{"answer":"The run did not establish which region has the strongest customer loyalty. The overall result was insufficient evidence, so no region could be confirmed as the leader.

The single claim it tested stayed unresolved: the data gave some support for the idea that loyalty differs across regions, but not enough to show that one region clearly ranked highest on the loyalty metric. The run used a ranking step, then stopped because the evidence was still too thin.

Two questions remained open: which region, if any, ranks highest on the available proxy for customer loyalty, and whether any apparent leader is stable or just a short-lived spike."}

